<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Agent Perimeter — MCP ecosystem census</title>
<style>{{ css|safe }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>MCP ecosystem census</h1>
<p class="mono">registry endpoint: {{ run.registry_endpoint }}</p>

<h2>Headline</h2>
<div class="strip">
<p data-testid="unknown-count"><strong>Artifact stratum.</strong> Of {{ artifact_n_examined }} npm/PyPI packages examined,
{{ artifact_agg.supports }} of {{ artifact_agg.n }} show published-artifact evidence of support
for <span class="mono">{{ revision }}</span> ({{ artifact_agg.does_not_support }} show no such
evidence, {{ artifact_agg.unknown }} unknown).</p>

{% if probe_agg is none %}
<p><strong>Live-discover stratum.</strong> Tier 3 remote-stratum sample: not yet run. This
report does not estimate live, ecosystem-wide support from artifact evidence alone — when Tier
3 runs, its result will appear here as its own, separately labelled figure.</p>
{% else %}
<p><strong>Live-discover stratum.</strong> Of a random sample of {{ probe_n }} remote MCP
servers, {{ probe_agg.supports }} answered a live discovery request in a way consistent with
support for <span class="mono">{{ revision }}</span>; {{ probe_agg.unknown }} unknown (no
answer, or excluded before a request was sent). A single unauthenticated probe can confirm
support; it can never confirm its absence, so this stratum does not report a does-not-support
count.</p>
{% endif %}

<p>These are two different populations, measured by two different methods. Neither figure is
combined with the other, and neither stands in for "the MCP ecosystem" as a whole.</p>
</div>

<h2>Collection window</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Started</th><td class="mono">{{ run.started_at.isoformat() }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Finished</th><td class="mono">{{ run.finished_at.isoformat() if run.finished_at else "in progress" }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Population</th><td class="num" data-testid="population-size">{{ run.population_size }}</td></tr>
<tr><th>Sample seed</th><td class="num" data-testid="sample-seed">{{ run.sample_seed }}</td></tr>
</table>
<p data-testid="fetch-failures">Fetch failures: {{ run.fetch_failures }}</p>

<h2>Artifact stratum</h2>
<p><strong>Method.</strong> {{ selection_method|safe }}</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Ecosystem</th><th class="num">Tier-2 target n</th><th class="num">Examined</th>
    <th class="num">Supports</th><th class="num">Does not support</th><th class="num">Unknown</th>
    <th class="num">Share</th></tr>
{% for eco, row in by_ecosystem.items() %}
<tr>
  <td class="mono">{{ eco }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ run.tier2_n }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.n_examined }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.does_not_support }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ row.aggregate.unknown }} unknown</td>
  <td class="num">{{ "n/a" if row.aggregate.share is none else "%.0f%%"|format(row.aggregate.share * 100) }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr>
  <td class="mono"><strong>pooled (both ecosystems)</strong></td>
  <td class="num">—</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_n_examined }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.does_not_support }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ artifact_agg.unknown }} unknown</td>
  <td class="num">{{ "n/a" if artifact_agg.share is none else "%.0f%%"|format(artifact_agg.share * 100) }}</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="deriv">Tier-2 target n is per ecosystem, not pooled: up to
<span data-testid="tier2-n">{{ run.tier2_n }}</span> npm packages and up to {{ run.tier2_n }}
PyPI packages are independently drawn at random (seed {{ run.sample_seed }}) within each
ecosystem before any artifact is fetched.</p>

<h2>Live-discover stratum</h2>
{% if probe_agg is none %}
<p>Tier 3 remote-stratum sample: not yet run. No live-discover records exist in this
publication.</p>
{% else %}
<table>
<tr><th class="num">Sampled</th><th class="num">Supports</th><th class="num">Unknown</th></tr>
<tr>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_n }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_agg.supports }}</td>
  <td class="num">{{ probe_agg.unknown }} unknown</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p class="deriv">No share/percentage is reported for this stratum. "Does not support" is
structurally always 0 here — a single probe can confirm support, never its absence (see
"live-discover sample" below) — so a supports-over-n ratio would look fully positive even when
most of the sample never answered at all. {{ probe_agg.unknown }} of the {{ probe_n }} sampled
hosts never answered a request, or were excluded before one was sent: that non-response count
is the number that matters here, not a derived percentage.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Terms</h2>
<dl data-testid="term-definitions">
{% for term, definition in term_definitions.items() %}
<dt><strong>{{ term }}</strong></dt>
<dd>{{ definition|safe }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
</dl>

<footer>
<h2>Methodology</h2>
<p>Tool version <span class="mono">{{ run.tool_version }}</span>, method hash
<span class="mono">{{ run.method_hash }}</span>. A changed collection method cannot silently
reuse this label - see the changelog below.</p>
<p>Raw data (digest-keyed, no names or URLs): <a href="records.csv">records.csv</a>. Reproduce
every number above with <a href="../../../analysis/census_analysis.py">analysis/census_analysis.py records.csv</a> -
no database, no salt, no API key required.</p>
<p>Secrets or other sensitive findings from this collection are handled per the
<a href="../../security.md">disclosure policy</a>, never published here.</p>
<p>Results are versioned, never overwritten: see the
<a href="../CHANGELOG.md">census changelog</a>.</p>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
